{"Success":true,"Data":{"State":"open","OpenTime":0,"CloseTime":0,"IsApproved":true,"IsPinned":false,"IsDeleted":false,"IsHidden":false,"IsArchived":false,"IsFollowing":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanReply":true,"CanFollow":true,"TotalPosts":7,"QueuedPosts":0,"DeletedPosts":0,"HasUnreadPosts":true,"HasAttachments":false,"Views":2040,"MovedTo":null,"MovedOn":0,"FirstPostId":292503,"Rating":0,"RatingHits":0,"Starter":{"Id":208141,"Name":"heather007","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-208141.gif?_r=0","PhotoWidth":100,"PhotoHeight":75,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"StartDate":1209968843,"LastPoster":{"Id":284110,"Name":"joliebrad20","Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"IsOnline":false},"PollState":"0","LastVote":0,"ForumId":74,"Preview":{"Id":292503,"PostDate":1209968843,"PostContent":"I got 200 3x4 organza bags from my fiance's aunt but they are the wrong colour. They are lavander...","Author":{"Signature":"<div class=\"post-sig post-sig-limit shazam usersig-click\"><div class=\"reparse-sig-lineheight\"><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href=\"http:\/\/i281.photobucket.com\/albums\/kk204\/francisandheather\/weddingblinkie1-2.png\">http:\/\/i281.photobucket.com\/albums\/k...blinkie1-2.png<\/a><br><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;10732;130\/st\/20090212\/e\/Our+Barcelo+Wedding\/k\/0ca1\/event.png\">http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt...0ca1\/event.png<\/a><br><br><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href=\"http:\/\/www.mywedding.com\/francisandheather\">http:\/\/www.mywedding.com\/francisandheather<\/a><br><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href=\"http:\/\/francisandheather.shutterfly.com\/\">http:\/\/francisandheather.shutterfly.com\/<\/a><span> password: wedding<\/span><\/div><\/div>","Email":"francisandheather@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1199572995,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-208141.gif?_r=0","PhotoWidth":100,"PhotoHeight":75,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"heather007","Id":208141,"Name":"heather007","IsOnline":false}},"Posts":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":true,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":15795,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"edba1b66f74cbbbb1c53108ec1b7eb5b","RawContent":"I got 200 3x4 organza bags from my fiance&#039;s aunt but they are the wrong colour. They are lavander. I&#039;m wondering if I&#039;m able to dye them another colour, and if this is possible, how? I&#039;m wanting something along the lines of turquoise, fushia, or green.\n \n Thanks!!!! :)\n \n ~~","Attachments":[],"Id":292503,"PostDate":1209968843,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                I got 200 3x4 organza bags from my fiance's aunt but they are the wrong colour. They are lavander. I'm wondering if I'm able to dye them another colour, and if this is possible, how? I'm wanting something along the lines of turquoise, fushia, or green.<br \/> <br \/> Thanks!!!! <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><br \/> <br \/> ~~\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div class=\"post-sig post-sig-limit shazam usersig-click\"><div class=\"reparse-sig-lineheight\"><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href=\"http:\/\/i281.photobucket.com\/albums\/kk204\/francisandheather\/weddingblinkie1-2.png\">http:\/\/i281.photobucket.com\/albums\/k...blinkie1-2.png<\/a><br><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;10732;130\/st\/20090212\/e\/Our+Barcelo+Wedding\/k\/0ca1\/event.png\">http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt...0ca1\/event.png<\/a><br><br><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href=\"http:\/\/www.mywedding.com\/francisandheather\">http:\/\/www.mywedding.com\/francisandheather<\/a><br><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href=\"http:\/\/francisandheather.shutterfly.com\/\">http:\/\/francisandheather.shutterfly.com\/<\/a><span> password: wedding<\/span><\/div><\/div>","Email":"francisandheather@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1199572995,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-208141.gif?_r=0","PhotoWidth":100,"PhotoHeight":75,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"heather007","Id":208141,"Name":"heather007","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":15795,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"10c834a025e916c86cb98174e388da93","RawContent":"It will totally depend on the type of organza. If it&#039;s a natural fiber (silk), then it may be possible. But if you&#039;ve got a synthetic (which, given they are gift bags is likely the case), then it will be much tougher if not impossible. And even if you get the color on the fabric, it may rub off.\n \n Your best bet is to try one out. Given that lavender (purple) is a combo of blue and red, you probably want to avoid green as it may turn them brown (purple+green=brown). \n \n Of the colors you suggested, fushia may be your best bet. Turquoise may still have a slight purple-ish tint.","Attachments":[],"Id":292669,"PostDate":1209996890,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                It will totally depend on the type of organza. If it's a natural fiber (silk), then it may be possible. But if you've got a synthetic (which, given they are gift bags is likely the case), then it will be much tougher if not impossible. And even if you get the color on the fabric, it may rub off.<br \/> <br \/> Your best bet is to try one out. Given that lavender (purple) is a combo of blue and red, you probably want to avoid green as it may turn them brown (purple+green=brown). <br \/> <br \/> Of the colors you suggested, fushia may be your best bet. Turquoise may still have a slight purple-ish tint.\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>Happily married since 2008<\/p>\n<p>Allurements by Rebecca - Destination Wedding Invitations and more","Email":"rebecca@allurementsbyrebecca.com","IpAddress":"8.28.19.75","GroupId":46,"GroupName":"VIP Member","JoinDate":1199300280,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-208096.gif?_r=0","PhotoWidth":100,"PhotoHeight":100,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"becks","Id":208096,"Name":"becks","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":15795,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"e389a769b738eddfdf9286aa7c032f65","RawContent":"go to &lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=\"http:\/\/www.ritdye.com\"&gt;www.ritdye.com&lt;\/a&gt;\n \n as long as they have less than 50% polyester, they will take full color, any more than that and they will take some color, but won&#039;t be as bold.","Attachments":[],"Id":292789,"PostDate":1210003040,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                go to <a href='http:\/\/www.ritdye.com' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>www.ritdye.com<\/a><br \/> <br \/> as long as they have less than 50% polyester, they will take full color, any more than that and they will take some color, but won't be as bold.\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p><strong><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/bestdestinationwedding.com\/forum\/blogs\/erinb\">Visit My BDW Blog!<\/a><\/strong><br><strong><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/21100-couples-swept-away-review-insanely-long-and-detailed\/\">My CSA Wedding Review<\/a><\/strong><br><strong><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/20334-erinbs-csa-pro-pics-better-late-than-never\/\">Wedding Pictures<\/a><\/strong> & <strong><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/20335-erinbs-ttd-pic-heavy\/\">My TTD<\/a><\/strong><br><strong><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/18150-erinbs-planning-thread\/\">My Planning Thread<\/a><\/strong><\/p>\n","Email":"arynn2@aol.com","IpAddress":"74.138.76.73","GroupId":46,"GroupName":"VIP Member","JoinDate":1196792400,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-208007.gif?_r=0","PhotoWidth":71,"PhotoHeight":100,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"ErinB","Id":208007,"Name":"ErinB","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":15795,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"0a53f8077f6923f54f94f751fbc2662c","RawContent":"Thanks ladies, I look forward to trying it out. \n \n ~~","Attachments":[],"Id":293291,"PostDate":1210029050,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                Thanks ladies, I look forward to trying it out. <br \/> <br \/> ~~\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div class=\"post-sig post-sig-limit shazam usersig-click\"><div class=\"reparse-sig-lineheight\"><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href=\"http:\/\/i281.photobucket.com\/albums\/kk204\/francisandheather\/weddingblinkie1-2.png\">http:\/\/i281.photobucket.com\/albums\/k...blinkie1-2.png<\/a><br><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;10732;130\/st\/20090212\/e\/Our+Barcelo+Wedding\/k\/0ca1\/event.png\">http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt...0ca1\/event.png<\/a><br><br><a da